WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.850
- With Encanto you celebrated
the Hispanic family

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.820
and generational trauma
was kind of a major theme.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:06.750
- Yeah. Well, it's funny.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.070
I remember talking to you,

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:09.930
I think the week before it came out.

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:12.990
- Dude, I love you so much.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:14.100
You're so talented.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.420
I don't think you know a person

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.792
that's seen that movie more
than myself because of my kids.

00:00:17.792 --> 00:00:18.870
(Lynn and audience laughing)

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.450
- I remember the week
before it came out also,

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:25.947
I did your show and I met
someone and his name was Bruno,

00:00:25.947 --> 00:00:28.413
and I said, "You're not
gonna understand this yet,

00:00:28.413 --> 00:00:30.420
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.520
but I'm so sorry.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.630
I'm just- just remember I
said, I'm sorry in advance."

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.551
- [Kelly] It's like any girl named Jolene?

00:00:38.551 --> 00:00:39.840
(audience laughing)
- Yeah. Jolenes

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:40.673
or Brunos,
- Or Felicia.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.170
Elisas, I am sorry.
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:45.570
- I love that. That's hysterical.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.010
But speaking of Encanto,

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.320
is it true that Bruno
originally had a different name?

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.780
- Yeah. Bruno in the early
drafts was named Oscar.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:53.790
- [Kelly] I can't hear that now.

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:54.623
- Yeah well-

00:00:54.623 --> 00:00:56.288
♪ You don't talk about Oscar ♪

00:00:56.288 --> 00:00:57.480
♪ Car, car, car ♪

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:58.313
- [Lynn] It doesn't sing.

00:00:58.313 --> 00:00:59.760
- [Kelly] It's yeah- Bruno sounds good.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.500
- [Lynn] And then they found
out that Oscar Madrigal

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.090
was like a super common name

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:05.490
or like a taken name in Colombia.

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:07.980
And so they gave me like
three other finalists.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.050
And as soon as I saw
Bruno, I was like, got it.

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:10.883
- Yeah.

00:01:10.883 --> 00:01:11.970
- I got the whole song.
- Yeah.

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.890
- I got Bruno and I can
play with the no, no, no.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.150
And I'm done.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:15.983
Thank you for writing-
- Great vowel.

00:01:15.983 --> 00:01:16.816
- the song for me. Great vowel.

00:01:16.816 --> 00:01:18.570
- Just a great vowel to sing, really.

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:19.403
- Yeah

00:01:19.403 --> 00:01:21.150
- I like to change those up
sometimes and they're like

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:22.392
that's not how you pronounce it.

00:01:22.392 --> 00:01:23.433
I don't care.

